# Build context for src/ImageSeg.Web/Dockerfile is the repo root (deploy/docker-compose.yml
# uses `context: ..`). Without this file, `COPY src/ src/` copies every local bin/ and obj/
# folder too - including project.assets.json from whatever machine last ran `dotnet build` or
# `dotnet ef migrations add` outside Docker. That file bakes in absolute, host-specific NuGet
# fallback-folder paths (e.g. Windows' "C:\Program Files (x86)\...\NuGetPackages"), which then
# overwrite the container's own fresh `dotnet restore` output and break `dotnet publish
# --no-restore` with a NuGet.Packaging.Core.PackagingException on Linux.
bin/
obj/
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.idea/
.vs/
**/*.user

deploy/
loadtest/
